# Third-party material in MissionPlannerRust

MissionPlannerRust is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 (the file
LICENSE; SPDX GPL-3.0-only), and NOTICE says what it is. This file records what it carries from
others: the work it derives from, the code and data that reached it through that work, the
programs whose behaviour it reproduces, and the Rust crates its binaries are built from. Where a
licence asks for its notice to travel with the code, the notice is here, verbatim; the GNU
licences' texts are LICENSE and <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

Each entry names where the material sits in ( the original ) Mission Planner's tree (paths under
https://github.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner, commit `efb0801`) and where in this one.

## 1. Mission Planner

**Mission Planner** - Copyright (C) 2010-2024 Michael Oborne and contributors -
<https://github.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner> - GNU General Public License version 3 (the
repository's `COPYING.txt` is the licence text; `Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs` gives the copyright
line).

MissionPlannerRust is a derivative of it: every ported Rust module names the C# file and lines it
follows (`// C#: <file>:<lines>`), `ledger/ledger.csv` records every C# file's state, and NOTICE
is the section 5(a) statement of what was changed. Carried from its tree as data rather than code:

- `assets/images/*.png` - the drawn images of its `Resources/` and of the SITL page's `.resx`,
  each listed with its Designer site in `crates/mp-gui/src/pictures.rs`. Its product photographs
  (`Resources/*.jpg`: a Cube, a power module, a MinimOSD, an airspeed sensor, a sonar, an optical
  flow sensor) are the makers' pictures, not Mission Planner's to license, and are not carried.
- `assets/i18n/` - the strings of its `.resx` files, as Fluent files that `cargo xtask
  codegen-resx` generates.
- `assets/acsimplepids.xml`, `crates/mp-mission/assets/camerasBuiltin.xml`,
  `crates/mp-log/assets/graphs/*.xml`, `crates/mp-firmware/data/FirmwareHistory.txt` - its data
  files, byte for byte.
- `crates/mp-kml/assets/block_plane_0.dae` - its 3D plane model, a Google SketchUp 7 export.
- `crates/mp-script/src/clr/mavlink_enums.py` - the MAVLink enumerations as its generated
  `Mavlink.cs` has them (and see MAVLink, below).
- `testdata/` - recordings made with it and sample files from its tree, as test fixtures, beside
  this work's own.

