## 3. Rust crates

The binaries are built from the crates below, fetched by Cargo; each is used under its own
licence, every one of them compatible with the GNU GPL version 3, and `deny.toml` is the list
of licences admitted. Their texts are in the crates' own sources under `~/.cargo/registry` and
in their repositories.

**gpui** and its companions (`gpui`, `gpui_macros`, `collections`, `util`, `sum_tree`,
`refineable`, `media`, `http_client`, ...) are Zed Industries' UI framework
(<https://github.com/zed-industries/zed>, Apache License 2.0), used at the git commit the table
names; `calloop` is Zed's fork, at the commit gpui's own workspace patches it to. None of Zed's
GPL-licensed application crates (`ui`, `editor`, ...) is used.

**RustPython** (`rustpython-vm`, `rustpython-pylib`, ...) is under the MIT licence; the Python
standard library it carries (`rustpython-pylib`) and its documentation strings
(`rustpython-doc`) are under the Python Software Foundation licence (PSF-2.0), as is `pymath`;
`mt19937` carries the Mersenne Twister's three-clause BSD terms (Matsumoto and Nishimura,
1997-2002). The four `malachite` crates are under the GNU LGPL version 3, whose additional
permissions the GPL's section 7 lets this work remove.

